<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roccagloriosa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roccagloriosa is a village in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilento">Cilento</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, near which lies a fortified Lucanian settlement of the 4th century BCE. Excavations there have revealed defensive walls, houses and rich tombs, making it one of the best-studied Lucanian hill towns and an important source for the society of the Lucanians.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roccagloriosa.jpg" alt="Roccagloriosa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Geofix · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roccagloriosa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
